# The legacy extract files are byte-exact evidence. Their SHA-256 checksums are
# recorded in data/legacy/MANIFEST.json and are reconciled by control REC-C01.
#
# Git's automatic line-ending normalisation would rewrite CRLF to LF on checkout
# and silently invalidate every one of those checksums. These files are also
# Latin-1 encoded, not UTF-8. Marking them -text stops Git touching either.
#
# This is the same integrity concern the pack documents under ALCOA+ 'Original':
# a stored record must survive transport unaltered, and version control is
# transport.
data/legacy/*.txt -text
data/legacy/MANIFEST.json -text

# Evidence records are generated artefacts; keep them stable too.
evidence/*.json -text
data/_oracle/*.json -text
